Sirtuin family members display distinct deacylase activities (
Table 1
;
Bheda et al., 2015
) and protein targets (
Nakagawa et al., 2009
) despite a high degree of conservation across isoforms in their sequence and structure (
Yuan and Marmorstein, 2012
;
Bheda et al., 2015
). Indeed, all seven sirtuins contain a core catalytic domain harboring a four-coordinate cysteine Zn
2+
finger (the Zn
2+
-tetrathiolate subdomain) with a structurally adjacent acyl-lysine binding pocket (
Figure 1
). Likewise, each sirtuin has an antiparallel β-sheet-rich Rossmann-fold subdomain that binds NAD
+
.
