Sirt3 glutathionylation has been observed in animal models. Sirt3 is glutathionylated
in vivo
in the aorta and kidney of hypertensive mice, which correlated with increased acetylation of the Sirt3 substrate SOD2, suggesting Sirt3 deacetylase activity is inhibited
in vivo
under inflammatory conditions (
